abstract: >-
  Analysis code and generated result datasets for a metabolite-aware
  pharmacokinetic simulation of missed imatinib doses in chronic myeloid
  leukemia. A two-compartment parent model coupled to a long-lived active
  metabolite (N-desmethyl-imatinib, CGP74588) is used to test whether the
  metabolite increases imatinib's forgiveness of missed doses at 400 and
  600 mg once daily. Version 1.1.0 (response to peer review) adds conditional
  and trajectory-based endpoints, published-model benchmarks and extended
  sensitivity analyses. Running Rscript R/run_all.R regenerates every reported
  value, table and figure.
keywords:
  - imatinib
  - CGP74588
  - pharmacokinetic forgiveness
  - medication adherence
  - chronic myeloid leukemia
  - therapeutic drug monitoring
